Clears out niri 26.04's dead imports as each new client buffer arrives.

The renderer keeps every buffer it imports until it cleans up, and it
cleans up only after drawing a frame. With every monitor off, or with the
screen locked and still, niri draws nothing while clients go on sending
new buffers, and every one stays. On Intel's xe driver each import also
holds a file descriptor, so a terminal redrawing a spinner piles up
thousands of them: 6,686 buffers, 66 GB, after three hours of a locked
laptop with its screen off. Cleaning up before each import keeps only
the imports of buffers clients still hold.

